 [para]
 
 The [cmd snit::type] [arg definition] block is a script that may
-contain the following definitions:
+contain the following definitions.  Note that the [arg definition] is
+evaluated in a separate interpreter used for compiling Snit types, not
+in the caller's interpreter, so it cannot refer to the caller's
+variables: e.g. [const {option -a -default $::a}] fails with
+[const {can't read "::a": no such variable}].  To use such a
+value, substitute it before the definition is evaluated, e.g. by
+building the [arg definition] with [cmd list] or [cmd {string map}], or
+set the option in the [cmd constructor] instead.
 
